 depositing a layer of photodefinable material on the inorganic hard mask over the array portion of the substrate; 
 removing the photodefinable material and the portion of the inorganic hard mask located over the periphery portion of the substrate; 
 removing a portion of the amorphous carbon layer in the exposed periphery of the substrate; 
 removing the inorganic hard mask resulting in a thicker layer of amorphous carbon over the array portion than the periphery portion; 
 depositing a second inorganic hard mask over the layer of amorphous carbon; 
 performing photolithography on the memory device; and 
 high aspect ratio plasma oxide etching. 



     2. The method of  claim 1 , further comprising:
 adjusting the portion of amorphous carbon remaining over the substrate depending on consumption of the amorphous carbon during high aspect ratio etching. 



